When you visit [https://example.com/about](https://example.com/about), your browser sends plain-text headers like this:

GET /about HTTP/1.1
Host: example.com
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64)
Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml

GET: The action verb (HTTP Method).

/about: The path to the specific resource requested.

HTTP/1.1: The protocol version.

Host:: The server domain name.
